// Pseudo-code for tenant deletion
function deleteTenant(tenantId) {
  purgePubSub(tenantId);
  deleteStorageObjects(tenantId);
  dropBigQueryPartitions(tenantId);
  verifyDeletion(tenantId);
  generateAuditReport(tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to architect scalable per-tenant security at the API boundary without expensive per-tenant VPCs, leveraging policy-as-code and strong observability. It probes how to bind identity, authorization, and data-access controls across managed services, plus testing and rollback strategies.

## Key Concepts

- API gateway security without per-tenant VPCs
- IAP/OAuth2 for per-tenant identity
- Policy-as-code with OPA for tenant-scoped rules
- Middleware enforcement in Cloud Run and tenant tagging in logs
- CMEK key management and VPC Service Controls for egress protection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example pseudo-middleware sketch
function authorize(req, res, next) {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const valid = opa.eval({tenant, action: req.method, path: req.path});
  if (!valid) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for tenant leakage during canary?
- What are the risks of using a single GCP project for all tenants and how would you mitigate?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design per-tenant privacy controls in a real-world multi-tenant GCP SaaS, balancing performance, data isolation, and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time data redaction with Cloud DLP integrated into Dataflow pipelines
- Per-tenant Cloud Storage buckets and BigQuery datasets with CMEK-managed encryption
- IAM Conditions for tenant-scoped least-privilege access controls
- Synthetic-tenant CI validation with automated rollback on policy violations

## Code Example
```terraform
# Per-tenant IAM condition binding
resource "google_project_iam_binding" "tenant_access" {
  project = var.project_id
  role    = "roles/storage.objectViewer"
  members = ["serviceAccount:${var.analyst_sa}"]
  condition {
    title       = "tenant_isolation_${var.tenant_id}"
    description = "Restrict access to tenant ${var.tenant_id} data only"
    expression  = "resource.labels.tenant_id == '${var.tenant_id}'"
  }
}

# Per-tenant Cloud Storage bucket with CMEK
resource "google_storage_bucket" "tenant_bucket" {
  name     = "${var.project_id}-data-${var.tenant_id}"
  location = var.region
  encryption {
    default_kms_key_name = google_kms_crypto_key.tenant_key.id
  }
  labels = {
    tenant_id = var.tenant_id
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical containment design across IAM, network perimeters, key management, and rollback validation using synthetic tenants.

## Key Concepts
- IAM conditions for tenant isolation
- Perimeter controls: PSC/VC and VPC Service Controls
- CMEK rotation and data-key isolation
- Automated rollback with synthetic tenants and validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: conditional binding to isolate tenant access
const policy = { bindings: [] };
policy.bindings.push({
  role: "roles/storage.objectViewer",
  members: ["user:tenant-a@example.com"],
  condition: {
    title: "Tenant Access Restriction",
    description: "Restrict access to tenant-specific resources",
    expression: "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/buckets/tenant-a-')"
  }
});
```
